			{
				"id": "HI-W2-1",
				"severity": "nit",
				"key": "ui.chat.run_details.state.interrupted",
				"finding": "Meaning correct, but glossary drift: the new state word 'बाधित' (also used in ui.chat.run_details.tally.interrupted) differs from the existing hi rendering of 'interrupted' in the transcript (ui.chat.canonical.transcript.interrupted / tool_row.outcome.interrupted = 'रोका गया', notice.interrupted = 'बीच में रोका गया'), so the same child can read 'बाधित' in run details and 'रोका गया' in the transcript. 'बाधित' is clear and distinct from paused 'रुका हुआ', so this does not gate. Suggestion if harmonising later: 'बीच में रोका गया' / tally one {# बीच में रोका गया} other {# बीच में रोके गए}. Disposition: non-gating; deferrable."
			},
			{
				"id": "HI-W2-2",
				"severity": "nit",
				"key": "ui.chat.canonical.supplement.status.preparing",
				"finding": "The new supplement copy names the feature 'हाइलाइट्स' (status.preparing/cancelled/failed, explanation.*), while the existing notice ui.notices.files.highlights_update_failed uses 'हाइलाइट' ('हाइलाइट अपडेट नहीं हो सके'). Both are acceptable loanword plurals (existing hi also uses 'जॉब्स') and agreement inside each string is correct (masculine plural: तैयार हो रहे हैं, रद्द किए गए, रुक गए); no existing ui.chat.canonical.supplement key names the feature, so the context instruction has no stronger anchor. Disposition: non-gating; harmonise in a later pass if desired."
			}
		]
	},
